-- title:
--   Modular unit at the far branch of the j-finite chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an integer $M$ with $M \neq 0$, $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a $\{p\}$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L(\!(q)\!)$ over $L$ generated by the coefficientwise image, along $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with $q$-expansion $q^{-1}\,\mathrm{jNumQ}(q)$, and let $\mathcal{O} =$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.chartAlgFin A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L135) be the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$. Let $u, u' \in \mathcal{O}$ have $q$-expansions the image of $\Delta(q)/\Delta(q^p)$ and $p^{12}$ times its inverse, respectively. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ consisting exactly of those $f$ for which $f \cdot y = x$ in $L(\!(q)\!)$ for some $x, y \in A[\![q]\!]$ with $y$ nonzero modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ (the Gauss valuation). Let $\sigma$ be an $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$ with $\sigma(u) = u'$, let $W_1$ be the valuation subring $\sigma^{-1}(W_0)$, i.e. $f \in W_1 \iff \sigma f \in W_0$, and let $P_1$ be a prime ideal of $\mathcal{O}$ consisting exactly of those $b$ whose image in $K$ is a non-unit of $W_1$. Then $u \in P_1$, $u' \notin P_1$, and for every monic $g \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$ of positive degree the element $g(u')$ does not lie in $P_1$.
--
--   This is the behaviour of the Siegel-type modular unit $u = \Delta(q)/\Delta(q^p)$ and of its companion $u' = p^{12}/u$ at the branch $W_1$ of the special fibre obtained from the Gauss valuation by transport along the Atkin–Lehner-type automorphism $\sigma$ of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$: on the $j$-finite chart, $u$ vanishes at the centre of $W_1$ while $u'$ and all monic integral polynomial expressions in $u'$ are units there. It feeds the construction of finite étale level sets of the modular unit on that chart in [`ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_finite_etale_quotient_span_aeval_chartAlgFin_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_finite_etale_quotient_span_aeval_chartAlgFin_twoChartModel_x1_mul).
